    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Today, there are two Detroits. One Detroit is the Detroit that has existed for the last few decades, an overwhelmingly black city with a large portion of the population below the poverty line. The Second Detroit is \"Detroit 2.0\" which consists of 7.2 of the 142.9 square miles of Detroit now has outdoor cafes, beautifully landscaped streets, street furniture, trendy restaurants, tech companies, and startups. “Detroit 2.0” does not focus on the low income, mostly black residents whose fate is crucial to the success of the city’s future. Only by working together to implement policies that ensure the low income residents of Detroit benefit from the new investments will Detroit be able to truly improve and create positive change in the city overall.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
